{"task":"Keep the ports a previous install chose, and step past ones already taken","goals":"Stop a re-install rendering a wildcard server on an admin port something else holds","status":"Waiting","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T02:25:37Z","body":"Found while preparing to run the new installer on this machine, before running it: it\nwould have installed a wildcard server that never came up.\n\nThe installer's built-in ADMIN_PORT is 2019. This machine's config records 2021, because\nseasonal-drops' own Caddy holds 2019 and somebody moved ldev off it by hand. The installer\ndid not read the existing config, so a re-install would have written 2019 back and rendered\na Caddyfile with `admin localhost:2019` — a port already taken. Caddy binds its admin API\nat startup and EXITS when it cannot, with no warning and no fallback, so the symptom is a\ndaemon that installs cleanly, reports success, and serves nothing.\n\nTwo changes, because the two failures are different:\n\nA previous install's ports are now carried forward as the starting point. They are a\nDECISION, not a default — the only reason a config says 2021 is that somebody hit this and\nfixed it — and resetting them re-creates the collision they solved.\n\nThen the ports are checked for real, and stepped past if taken. This is what makes it\nself-healing rather than merely non-destructive: a fresh machine with no config still gets\nthe defaults, and still gets moved off them if something else answers there.\n\nThe check happens AFTER the takedown, not before, and the config file moved with it. Before\nthe takedown, a port held by the very job about to be removed looks taken, and the installer\nwould skip a port that was about to be free. Moving the config write later is safe because\nthe only thing that reads it — `ldev render` — runs two steps further on.\n\ntest/install-ports.test.sh asserts both halves: a config's ports survive a re-install, a\nfresh machine keeps the defaults, a taken port is stepped over (including the real\n2019-is-held case), a free one is returned unchanged, and a search that finds nothing free\ngives back what it was asked for rather than hanging or returning something taken.\n\nThe busy-port cases use a stubbed port_busy. Binding a real socket from a backgrounded\nprocess inside the test proved flaky — the process was alive and `nc -z` still reported the\nport free — and that flakiness is not what is under test. The real port_busy is one line,\nverified by hand against a live listener; what needed asserting is that free_port_from\nsteps past a taken port rather than returning it.\n","parent_commit":"1a94e18097adb926d23f249164d307df31359d81","repo":"brave-cedar-fb33","pct":"71","tasks":[{"id":"carry","content":"Carry a previous install's ADMIN_PORT/ASK_PORT/SITE_PORT_BASE forward instead of resetting to defaults","status":"completed"},{"id":"probe","content":"Step past an admin or ask port something else already holds","status":"completed"},{"id":"order","content":"Choose ports and write the config after the takedown, so a port about to be freed is not skipped","status":"completed"},{"id":"tests","content":"test/install-ports.test.sh — 9 assertions over carry-forward and stepping","status":"completed","created_at":"2026-09-10T01:14:35.832Z","status_at":"2026-09-10T01:14:35.832Z"},{"id":"docs","content":"README: the tests listing and the ADMIN_PORT/ASK_PORT config rows","status":"completed","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:08:36.006Z","status_at":"2026-09-09T19:22:30.481Z"},{"id":"migrate","content":"Run the installer on this machine to replace com.bryce.caddy-matsu with the wildcard daemon","status":"pending","human_reason":"Needs sudo and a terminal: this session has neither (sudo requires a password here, stdin is not a tty), so the installer would abort partway. It is also root-owned and briefly takes matsu.ldev offline while 443 changes hands. Run /Users/bryce/Projects/ldev/install.sh interactively; it now finds com.bryce.caddy-matsu, offers to remove it, keeps com.bryce.caddy-seasonal-drops, and picks an admin port that is actually free.","created_at":"2026-09-10T02:16:21.558Z","status_at":"2026-09-10T02:16:21.558Z"},{"id":"rehome-run","content":"Run ldev rehome against the three real WordPress sites","status":"pending","human_reason":"Rewrites live site data: 16,224 database rows for seasonal-drops alone, plus WP_HOME/WP_SITEURL in wp-config.php. The command refuses to run without a terminal to confirm on, so an agent cannot execute it and should not be given --yes on someone's real databases.","created_at":"2026-09-09T19:22:30.481Z","status_at":"2026-09-09T19:22:30.481Z"}],"agent":"claude-code","changelog":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","code_quality":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","vulnerabilities":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","code_style_suggestions":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","reusability":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","system_compatibility":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","sessions":[{"provider":"claude","id":"3e8f56a2-7837-42a5-adfb-4e072f3876ee","title":"https://sites.ldev/ (or any other name I put) doesn't auto redirect to the projects dashboard","linked_at":"2026-09-10T02:25:37Z"}],"review_run":{"state":"did_not_run","at":"2026-09-10T02:25:37Z","attempts":1,"reason":"Review skipped at the caller's request (--no-review / automatedReview: false)."}}
